	<div class="smallfont" style="margin-bottom:2px">Quote:</div>
	<table cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
	<tr>
		<td class="alt2" style="border:1px inset">
			
				<div>
					Originally Posted by <strong>Sunhome Ninja</strong>
					<a href="showthread.php?p=10659942#post10659942" rel="nofollow"><img class="inlineimg" src="images/buttons/viewpost.gif" border="0" alt="View Post" /></a>
				</div>
				<div style="font-style:italic">The Howler is ridiculous. <br />
<br />
Worst case you get an X/X for 3, and it's black so it dodges some removal (while weak to others) but most importantly, if you bestow it (to say, a Lifebane Zombie?) then it becomes a critter again after the guy its attached to dies, only even bigger!<br />
<br />
Not sure if I'd do 4-of, but it's easily a good 3-of. Sets up some nice devotion as well for the Merchant.</div>
			
		</td>
	</tr>
	</table>
</div>Worst case it's a 0/0 and dies/can't be cast profitably. Aside from the fact that you need to find a way to set it up to do anything, there's stuff like <a class="autocardhref" href="http://www.magiccards.info/query?q=%21Scavenging+Ooze" onclick="AutoCard('Scavenging Ooze'); return false;" title="Scavenging Ooze">Scavenging Ooze</a> and <a class="autocardhref" href="http://www.magiccards.info/query?q=%21Deathrite+Shaman" onclick="AutoCard('Deathrite Shaman'); return false;" title="Deathrite Shaman">Deathrite Shaman</a> in the format that love to eat creatures in the yard. It's a shame, the art on howler is fantastic no doubt.
		</div>
